      "id": 1,
      "text": "Higley takes its name from Stephen Weaver Higley, who bought 40 acres in 1905‑06 and had the town platted in 1928.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Higley%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The San Tan Historical Society runs Crossroads of Historic Higley, an oral‑history tour that invites locals to share their stories.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://makehigleyhistoric.blogspot.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mary Coffin Johnson’s 1896 book, The Higleys and Their Ancestry, traces Captain John Higley’s arrival in Connecticut in the late 17th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://makehigleyhistoric.blogspot.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The original Higley townsite was located on the southwest corner of the plotted 40‑acre parcel.",
